msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:59
#: 1390e302d2474e7d83c7eb78aada8666
msgid "Using the sensor with an AP Periph DroneCAN Node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:60
#: 227a8e5611e340c9b335787fba20fc6e
msgid "The USD1 is available in either CAN or Serial communication protocol versions. The USD1 CAN protocol is different than DroneCAN and hence requires a dedicated CAN port running this protocol. If the autopilot does not have a spare CAN port or spare serial port for connecting the USD1, but has a DroneCAN port setup, you can create another serial port in the system using an AP_Periph CAN node attached to the DroneCAN port. The USD1 MUST be the Serial version for this to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:62
#: 660ec65e32c14c7a9855218fd67f8204
msgid "To use the USD1 with a CAN Node like the Matek AP_Periph CAN Node L431, use the following set up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:64
#: 27d161ef17de4190a6a63833a356b1ff
msgid "First, flash the AP_Periph device with a firmware that has the rangefinder features. For the Matek AP_Periph CAN Node L431, the latest stable firmware is `here. <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AP_Periph/stable/MatekL431-Rangefinder/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:69
#: 45ff47e911664ccb92005c8ca427ebe0
msgid "Set the parameters in the CAN Node to the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:71
#: 174aaeb2a57b496ba791f6a264f17f6d
msgid "RNGFND_BAUDRATE = 115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:72
#: 1572a7062275454aa06fa64a2b7871c9
msgid "RNGFND_MAX_RATE = 50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:73
#: bd7f83149e474192b86f1aa5589b8b07
msgid "RNGFND_PORT = 1 (UART 2, i.e. TX2, RX2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:74
#: 64eba464671540abbf7b8a53201a2a12
msgid "RNGFND1_ORIENT = 0 (No matter what orientation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:75
#: bc621dcbebbc41e49295af5c35329cb0
msgid "RNGFND1_TYPE = 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:79
#: 590e3441015d4d0ca2e5dd6fe5f12303
msgid "RNGFND_PORT is indexed differently than the UARTs on the board. For RNGFND_PORT = 0, use RX1 and TX1 on the board, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:81
#: eb1b49b81614455bba5c08624f17a29d
msgid "Next, set the parameters on the autopilot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:83
#: 4af3d9d4737c45c09686c0f80b94c293
msgid "RNGFND1_TYPE = 24 (DroneCAN) Then Restart"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:84
#: d27db52320aa47eeab26d931474b64b4
msgid "RNGFND1_ORIENT = 25 (Down)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:85
#: ec1fc4b0738740bfa19308ce7803effa
msgid "RNGFND1_ADDR = 0 (For sensor_id = 0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-aerotenna-usd1.rst:89
#: 252c9c799cfb4b90a8f8cf8bd5f200c6
msgid "If there is more than one rangefinder in the system you will need to determine the Sensor ID for the USD1. Look in CAN inspector for a message \"uavcan_equiment_range_sensor_Measurement\" for its sensor_id."
msgstr ""
